  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Electoral Observation Mission (MOE) 2017-2021</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Valobservat&#xf6;rsuppdrag (MOE) 2017-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att bidra till &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngsprocessen genom att genomf&#xf6;ra demokratist&#xe4;rkande &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder som fr&#xe4;mjar reformen av det colombianska valsystemet genom att; 1) St&#xe4;rka samh&#xe4;llsorganisationer och lokala institutioner under &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngsprocessen genom &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder som syftar till att st&#xe4;rka informationsprocesser och initiativtagande hos medborgare; 2) St&#xe4;rka lokala institutioner genom b&#xe4;ttre f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else av korruption associerat till det colombianska valsystemet; 3) P&#xe5;verka reformprocesser som syftar till att st&#xe4;rka demokratin. Programmet f&#xe5;r 11197 645 SEK mellan &#xe5;ren 2017-2021.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention aims to contribute to the transition process towards the democratic strengthening through actions that promote the modernization of the Colombian electoral system by 1) Strengthening social organizations and local institutions during the transition process, through actions aimed to reinforce information processes, formation, and citizen action. 2) Strengthening local institutions through a better comprehension of corruption phenomena associated to the political-electoral system. 3) Influence reform processes of political and electoral matter, aiming for the strengthening of democracy. The program will receive 11 197 645 SEK between 2017-2021.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed at contributing to the process of transition towards democratic strengthening by promoting the modernization of the Colombian electoral system and the expansion of local and daily democracy.  
This includes three main outputs: 

1.Transition and democratic strengthening: it includes the electoral observation process, that will produce informational risk maps; the characterization of social dynamics of the post-conflict zones; and democratic quality assessment, that includes womens role in national and local politics, and the everyday democratic citizen participation.

2.Corruption, politics, and democracy: This objective seeks to strengthen the local institutions by offering a bigger comprehension of the corruption phenomena, associated to the political-electoral system and to create accountability measures between the elected officers and their voters.

3.Political influence society-state: The last objective aims to influence in the legal reforms and institutional adjustments that are required for the post-conflict scenario in political and electoral thematic.  Those actions will be supported in the research and analysis that the MOE performs throughout the country.</narrative>
  </description>
